  "notes": "|0>^4, |1>^4, |+>^4, |->^4 and |+i>^4 span the five-dimensional symmetric subspace (the six product stabilizer states |0>^n, |1>^n, |+->^n, |+-i>^n span Sym^n for n <= 5 and only a six-dimensional subspace beyond), so chi <= 5 at four copies for every single-qubit state; this is the generic value chi_4 = 5 of Lovitz and Steffan (arXiv:2110.07781, Section 1.3). Puts the cell at 4 <= chi(|sqrtT>^4) <= 5. Whether 4 is attained is open: the research survey's cap-4 MILP over the 36,720 four-qubit words did not finish in 600 s, and the rank-4 pivot-pair search of slice_lift.all_decompositions is the tool. Implied gamma log_2(5)/4 = 0.5805 against the published 1/2. For comparison chi(|T>^4) = 3 (edge orbit, lean tier) and chi(|H>^4) = 4."
